    "caveats": [
      "Residence time is exactly 6.0 s at 40 µL/min — this meets the ≥6 s requirement but leaves zero margin; if any flow pulsation or drift occurs the residence time drops below 6 s. Consider a slightly lower flow (e.g. 35 µL/min → ~6.9 s) if the shear target can tolerate a small reduction, or confirm the pump holds 40 µL/min precisely.",
      "HCMEC/D3 forms only a moderately restrictive BBB (TEER 100-240 Ω·cm², ~10× below physiological BBB ~1800-2000 Ω·cm²). Do not claim in-vivo BBB integrity; interpret permeability/TEER accordingly.",
      "Confirm the syringe pump can deliver 40 µL/min against ~2000 Pa (~20 mbar) backpressure — standard syringe pumps handle this easily, but verify tubing/connector ratings.",
      "Verify medium viscosity ≈ 1e-3 Pa·s (water-like); serum-supplemented medium may be slightly higher, which would raise shear above 1.0 Pa at fixed flow.",
      "Seed density 15,000 cells/cm² is an endothelial-typical assumption (HCMEC/D3 registry has no seeding density); verify monolayer formation and coverage in the lab.",
      "Confirm the drug does not bind significantly to PDMS/tubing (non-specific binding) before interpreting perfusion clearance data."
    ]
  },
